course: dictionary
lesson: 9901
title: Talk: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word talk can mean different things, and the words around it show you which one. «The baby is learning to talk.» Here talk means to say words. Ask yourself what the sentence is about, then choose the meaning that fits.
explain: «We talked for hours.» Here talk means to have a conversation with someone. Talk can also be a noun: «The firefighter gave a talk» means a speech to a group. Talk is a verb and a noun, so check which one the sentence needs.
explain: Talk also helps with feelings. «If you think a friend has stolen something, you have a duty to act, starting by talking to them or a trusted adult.» Talking to a trusted adult helps when you are sad, scared or worried.
fact: Talk means to say words, to have a conversation, or to discuss something.
fact: As a noun, a talk is a conversation or a speech to a group.
fact: The forms of the verb are talk, talks, talked and talking.
fact: Useful phrases include talk to, talk about, talk back, talk over, small talk and pep talk.
fact: «At his cousin's birthday they meet for real and nobody knows what to say; everyone talks at once.» Here talks means speaks.
exercise: «The baby is learning to talk.» What does talk mean here? | To give a speech to a crowd | To say words | *To say words, as in speaking for the first time | To have a conversation with a friend
exercise: «We talked for hours.» What does talked mean? | To throw a ball around | To sleep in a tent | To paint a picture | *To have a conversation
exercise: «The firefighter gave a talk.» What is a talk here? | A loud noise | *A speech to a group | A small bag
test: If you are sad or worried, who should you talk to? | Nobody, ever | The family dog | A stranger online | *A trusted adult
test: Which phrase means a light chat about nothing important? | Talk back | Talk over | *Small talk | Pep talk
exam: Choose the best meaning of talk in «Let's talk about it.» | To go to sleep | To shout loudly | *To discuss | To sing a song
